 # unreleased
 
+- Apply Unicode's Final_Sigma condition when lowercasing, in full: a `Σ` takes
+  its final form `ς` only when a cased character precedes it and none follows it,
+  in both directions across any run of case-ignorable characters. So
+  `"Σ".to_snake_case()` is now `"σ"`, `"1Σ".to_snake_case()` is now `"1σ"`,
+  `"AʼΣ".to_snake_case()` is now `"aʼς"` and `"ΑΣ1".to_snake_case()` is now
+  `"ας1"`. A word carrying a capital sigma is lowercased through
+  `str::to_lowercase`, so the two can no longer disagree; a word without one
+  still streams into the formatter without allocating.
+- Titlecase the first character of a word rather than uppercasing it, so
+  `"ß".to_upper_camel_case()` is now `"Ss"`, `"ﬄe".to_title_case()` is now
+  `"Ffle"`, `"ǳab".to_title_case()` is now `"ǲab"`, and Georgian Mkhedruli,
+  which has no titlecase, is left unchanged instead of being uppercased.
+  A Greek character carrying an iota subscript keeps the subscript rather than
+  raising it to a capital iota, so `"ᾀβ".to_title_case()` is now `"ᾈβ"` and
+  `"ᾲ".to_title_case()` is now `"Ὰ"` followed by U+0345.
+- Derive `Debug`, `Clone` and `Copy` on all eight `As*Case` wrappers, so a type
+  holding one can derive them too.
+- Honour the formatter's width, fill, alignment and precision in every
+  `As*Case` wrapper, so `format!("{:>20}", AsSnakeCase("aB"))` pads to twenty
+  columns as `format!("{:>20}", "a_b")` does. A wrapper formatted without any of
+  those parameters still streams into the formatter without allocating.
+
 # 0.5.0
 
 - Add `no_std` support.
